  <h3>Reminders</h3>
  <p>The parent writes a reminder as a sentence with a time and optional days, such as "On Tuesdays at 5 pm, pack the swimming bag." The house shows it on displays assigned to reminders. A button press dismisses it; otherwise it disappears at the end of its window, normally after thirty minutes. The press is not retained as evidence that the task was done.</p>

  <div class="pair">
    <figure>
      <img src="/images/reminder-teeth.webp" width="800" height="480" loading="lazy" alt="An illustrated toothbrush beside an Italian reminder to brush your teeth after lunch, around 1:30 pm." />
      <figcaption>An illustrated reminder. The Italian text is invented.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img src="/images/reminder-swimming.webp" width="800" height="480" loading="lazy" alt="A 5 pm reminder in Italian: Pack the swimming bag." />
      <figcaption>The text-only version, rendered by the display code with an invented Italian sentence.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p>On a display with several jobs, reminders take precedence over activity instructions, which take precedence over pictures. When the higher-priority content ends, the content underneath becomes visible again.</p>
